---
import Highlight from '../../layouts/Highlight.astro';
---

<Highlight slug="performance" lede="Fast pages are a product decision, not a finishing touch. On a large production app, I measure first, then cut what the browser does not need.">
	<section style="padding-top: 64px">
		<h2 class="lbl">What I did</h2>
		<ul class="bl">
			<li><span><b>Lighthouse audits</b> to find the biggest costs before touching code.</span></li>
			<li><span><b>Lower Total Blocking Time</b> by deferring third-party scripts and lazy-loading heavy UI providers.</span></li>
			<li><span><b>Render only what's visible</b>, and defer the rest to idle time.</span></li>
			<li><span><b>Code-splitting and lazy loading</b> so each route ships less JavaScript.</span></li>
		</ul>
	</section>
	<section style="padding-top: 64px">
		<h2 class="lbl">Results</h2>
		<div class="stat">
			<div><span class="n">[X] ms</span><span class="l">[METRIC — e.g. TBT before → after]</span></div>
			<div><span class="n">[X]</span><span class="l">[METRIC — e.g. LCP on mobile]</span></div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Highlight>
